=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The reported symptom — PC5 (172.16.10.5) unable to reach the 172.16.30.x design-group machines — is not reproducible in the current live state of the lab, and no historical mechanism that could have caused it was found.

**Affected component:** None confirmed. The inter-VLAN routing path between 172.16.10.0/24 and 172.16.30.0/24 runs through the multilayer switch `mswitch0`, which hosts all three VLANs (10, 20, 30) as routed OSPF interfaces (vlan10 at 172.16.10.254, vlan30 at 172.16.30.254).

**Mechanism:** A direct ping from pc5 → pc12 (172.16.30.12) currently completes with 0% loss and 1.67 ms RTT. The same probe was clean for every other tested pair (pc6–pc8 to pc12–pc14 all successful).

**Localization:** `mswitch0` is the single gateway bridging VLAN 10 and VLAN 30. OSPF snapshot confirms it is advertising both prefixes into area 0.0.0.0 with one Full adjacency toward router16 (its uplink); all 18 OSPF routes are present on every router in the fabric.

**Root cause:** No fault is present. The reported intermittent failure left no mechanism or trace — no ACL rules, no tc qdisc shaping, no OSPF adjacency instability, no interface flaps, no carrier-change history, and no resource pressure on any device in the path.

**Fix:** No corrective action required. If the user experiences the issue again, capture a timestamp and run `ping -c10 172.16.30.12` from pc5 immediately during the outage to obtain loss statistics for a time-correlated investigation.
=== END ===